+From 282ab87a9e195ce0a2d938d8f7500b8df5ed6424 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
+Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:22:55 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] sampling: K2-Horizon: mask the structural tool-call tags
+ while no native section is open
+
+With the history reasoning rendered in the generation tag (previous commit) the model no longer repeats the
+open tag or opens a Kimi call, but its first token after the reasoning open tag sometimes skips ahead:
+first-token probes (greedy, garage replay cuts 8/20/24): "<ifm|tool_call>" 0.62 / 0.10 / 0.15 and
+"</ifm|tool_calls>" 0.18 / 0.07 / 0.22 (bare call without its section opener, or a stray close), which
+parsed as reasoning-only turns (11/40 empty on the garage replay with the tag match alone; 0/40 with the
+old rendering, which instead repeated "<ifm|think>" 45-78%). The tags are single vocab tokens, so the guard,
+armed with tools, now masks every tool tag except the section opener while no native section is open;
+inside a section nothing is masked. Never masks the last candidate.
+
+Chat-level (tools offered, reasoning_effort low), live-session and garage replays, guard + normalisation:
+garage stream 0/40, live stream 0/60, garage non-stream 0/40 empty/stuck/Kimi (before: live stream
+16/60 Kimi + 1 empty + 2 stuck). Test: test-empty-reply-guard now also takes a second vocab (llama-bpe,
+special tokens standing in for the K2 tags). Satisfies K2-SAMP-01/07 extensions, K2-REPLAY-09 (design).
+
